From 1fb4e79ac54436ab909acd4a6c6cc75f370aad94 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mlgprorektm8 <67933lance@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 12:51:41 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 10/11] ryGT: buffer cache lock becomes shared/exclusive; stage
 reads take it shared (R1-R3)

- R1: the per-draw fields of the buffer cache (decode epoch, read capture, ahead uploads) are
  per thread, so the buffer stage no longer sees the recorder's job capture.
- R2: Common::RecursiveSharedMutex (re-entrant, shared inside exclusive; exclusive inside
  shared is fatal) replaces the recursive mutex; every existing hold stays exclusive.
- R3: the state SynchronizeMemory changes for read-only obtains has its own small locks
  (GPU-written ranges, hot-page streaks, pending ahead uploads, counters atomic); the stage's
  read obtains (perf 131) and the recorder's RecordAheadUploads take the cache lock shared.
Full Tokyo race: runs clean, 33.1 fps (within noise).

